  "_role": "spec",
  "_what": "Tyndall/volumetric-visibility decision matrix. Rows are display mode (W vs F), columns are density !beam / phase !scat / camera. Every arm additionally takes one !beamonly post-shot.",
  "_run": "powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\\opt-verify-taclight.ps1 -Spec tickets\\t-tyndall-matrix.json -Session W   (then -Session F after switching fullscreen:true and restarting the client; -Session W4 needs a human to press F4)",
  "_judgment": {
    "phase_caveat": "ALL 8 W arms are axis-collinear (thirdback/thirdfront keep the camera on the beam axis): center-pixel ph = 0.0160 = the phase minimum, identical to first person. Density pairs (W1 vs W2, W4 vs W5) therefore have almost no image leverage -- T7 already measured 0.072/255 for 0.05->0.5 at the minimum. Only off-center pixels gain (vertical edge x8.9, horizontal edge x14.4); a true x25 cell needs the camera OFF the beam axis (W4 F4, or an observer-instance remote light).",
    "W_has_beam_F_not": "display mode (window vs fullscreen) is the cause -- report as display口径, not a render regression (both sides are at the same phase minimum, so this comparison stays valid)",
    "W7_has_beam": "negative control failed: the ROI metric cannot separate beam from no-beam -- fix the metric before judging anything else",
    "W1_and_W5_no_beam": "product regression: escalate with the per-arm DIAG (count/flags/cam) as counter-evidence; still cannot distinguish \"density not uploaded\" from \"phase minimum\" until the vlParams dump patch (dumpLight0 +4 floats at offsets 80/84/88/92) is approved",
    "W4_free_visible_and_W4_free_005_not": "H4 can ONLY be judged in the freecam cell (camera off-axis): if beam 0.5 shows a cone there and 0.05 does not, the user-remembered Tyndall came from the manual !beam override (memory-only, cleared on restart)",
    "W2_vs_W3_difference_below_floor": "expected at the phase minimum -- do not read it as \"scat has no effect\"; re-test scat in a freecam/observer cell"
  },
  "_roi": "per shot: node tools/lumastats.js <png> --bbox x0,y0,x1,y1 (Y-mean of the cone region) ; floor = the 3 consecutive same-config shots of that arm; signal must exceed 3x floor; never use raw changed%",
  "scoped": "session display mode is asserted per arm via PNG IHDR; save=test; scene=wall; pose wall_front(2000.0,121.5,8.0,yaw180,pitch5); midnight + doDaylightCycle false + weather clear + doMobSpawning false; wait 20; single client; light on (flashlight) + !gun auto (dual lamp); tm=on (default) for every arm; every arm also takes one post-shot under !beamonly on",
